# Publish path

New posts go through `publish_own_video`. After trim, pass both the clipped Stream id and `p_source_stream_id` so the claim can move onto the clipped UID.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — extra client insert shapes when the RPC exists
await supabase.from("videos").insert(payload);

// ✅ GOOD — RPC is the write path (createVideo already does this first)
await supabase.rpc("publish_own_video", {
  p_cloudflare_stream_id: clippedUid,
  p_source_stream_id: sourceUid,
  // …
});
```

- Do not add more `videos.insert` attempts in `createVideo`.
- Clients must not insert/update `stream_upload_claims`. Only the Next Stream routes (service role) mint and mark claims `publishable`.
- Clip must transfer the claim onto the clipped UID. Status `uploaded` on the pre-clip source is not enough to publish.
- Video duration limits come from the claim’s `allowed_publish_seconds`.
- Pending upload queues are in-memory today. Prefer persisting/resuming over more in-memory retries. Do not assume a killed process still has the queue.
